This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}\ast u^p\right)~\text{in}~\mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^p\,dx=\mu^{\frac{p+2}{2}}\frac{\Gamma(1+p)\Gamma(5)}{2\Gamma(p+5)}~\text{on}~\mathbb{R}^4.
  \end{array}
  \end{split}
  \right.
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and parameters.
